ased with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I've never heard a compelling argument as to why Prometheans <b>should </b>be corpses. It's not prevalent in their inspiration (with two of the five Lineages explictly inspired by stories about animate statues), and seems to annex firmly Promethean archetypes, like Pinocchio and the Velveteen Rabbit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:51:30-07:00","id":274153,"title":"","content":"This is the first time I've heard of the Velveteen Rabbit, but one wikipedia article later I want to see him in the book or play him. Probably both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:58:49-07:00","id":274158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/273240-ptc-2e-open-development-has-started?p=274150#post274150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I've never heard a compelling argument as to why Prometheans <b>should </b>be corpses. It's not prevalent in their inspiration (with two of the five Lineages explictly inspired by stories about animate statues), and seems to annex firmly Promethean archetypes, like Pinocchio and the Velveteen Rabbit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much feel you on the Velveteen Rabbit being a great Promethean concept.<br /> <br /> Another great example of a Promethean from children's literature/folklore? Frosty the Snowman. He even has an obsessively Disquieted person hunting him down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T14:33:05-07:00","id":274174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/273240-ptc-2e-open-development-has-started?p=274150#post274150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I've never heard a compelling argument as to why Prometheans <b>should </b>be corpses. It's not prevalent in their inspiration (with two of the five Lineages explictly inspired by stories about animate statues), and seems to annex firmly Promethean archetypes, like Pinocchio and the Velveteen Rabbit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard a compelling argument that they shouldn't, given the horror(hell, explicitly body horror) genre we're in.<br /> <br /> But If I must, then it's by and large it's for the same reason I think adding Mummies to AKD's oath is lazy and boring-because it is. THere is a fresh edge added to the characters in line with the themes and genre when you make them corpse bodies rather than constructs. It's a point of atmosphere that adds subtly and richly to the entire affair. I'm not saying constructs can't be a thing, but it's not a central focus that having corpse bodies be the norm does. It's the little things that keep the narrative interesting.<br /> <br /> I mean, keep in mind, the cornerstone of this entire game, the thing that breathes life into all these other stories we're borrowing <i>is Frankenstein.</i><br /> <br /> Also I have a mild bias that basically says if I want to play a rock, I'll go play Changeling, but that is one hundred percent bullshit bias and shouldn't be factored in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T14:45:33-07:00","id":274177,"title":"","content":"I suppose there's an element of cognitive dissonance, Golem has a very particular connotation, and with the presence of the Unfleshed Prometheans are clearly <b>not </b>restricted to being human corpses. Certainly body horror is good and all, but the setting has ample room for more than one style of deformed terror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T14:50:44-07:00","id":274179,"title":"","content":"I'm pleased as punch the Unfleshed are in, but oddly that just reinforces the notion that the rest should be bodies. THe artifice aspect is covered strongly by one, no need to have multiple going dipping into the well.<br /> <br /> I'm something of a curmudgeon on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T14:53:32-07:00","id":274183,"title":"","content":"I also hope Golems aren't corpses, since that's antithetical to the source material. At the very least, I hope that Golems from clay are a viable option in the new core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:18:41-07:00","id":274192,"title":"","content":"See, to play Devil's Advocate, the same could be said the other way around. Three Lineages are decidedly corpses, no need for others. In the end I have to wonder if the material really matters at all. Promethean is, after all, a game of who you are not what you were. And a Frankenstein could just as easily be constructed of silicon and artificial tissues around a fresh vat grown brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 10-06-2014, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:33:47-07:00","id":274202,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I liked the way the Construct rules in <b>Magnum Opus</b> addressed this, for the most part: any Lineage can go with either flesh and bone or inarganic materials; and each Lineage has a particular class of materials that are most suitable as raw materials if you decide to go the Construct route. The Unfleshed are (probably) an exception to this; but for the most part, I wouldn\u2019t mind it if the creator had his choice of \u201cflesh golem\u201d or some other material \u2014 possibly even a mixture of the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:35:57-07:00","id":274204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/273240-ptc-2e-open-development-has-started?p=274150#post274150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I've never heard a compelling argument as to why Prometheans <b>should </b>be corpses. It's not prevalent in their inspiration (with two of the five Lineages explictly inspired by stories about animate statues), and seems to annex firmly Promethean archetypes, like Pinocchio and the Velveteen Rabbit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It evokes the horror element of their Creation, and the bodily alchemy themes that run through the whole game, and it's easy enough to assume that the horror-story Demiurge Gepetto, desperate for a child of his own, was chopping up the bodies of local children his in woodshop; or how Pygmalian was taking the most ideal parts from different women to make his &quot;physically perfect&quot; goddess, etc.<br /> <br /> Hunter: the Vigil: Mortal Remains has a story in its Promethean chapter about the Golem, where it suggests that the &quot;made from clay&quot; element is an oblique reference to human flesh having first come from clay (as Adam was made in Genesis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:42:33-07:00","id":274214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/273240-ptc-2e-open-development-has-started?p=273911#post273911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is. 5 basic Refinements, 5 complex.<br /> <br /> But I'll tell you more about that if &quot;Refinements&quot; wins the vote.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting... the obvious assumption to make is that the 5 &quot;basic&quot; Refinements are the five from the original core - but I'd argue Plumbum is pretty damn basic, and Mercuris is pretty damn complex, so a switch there would not surprise me at all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:42:33-07:00","id":274215,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the idea of a &quot;flesh golem&quot; or a copper statue Frankenstein, but if Lineages have a default or even a hard rule I'd like that default to be flesh Fraknenstines, clay Golems, etc. Both because it creates diversity - and a game that has creation as such a strong theme should have diversity for diversity is creativity - and because I like mythological accuracy. I know the WoD likes to say that myths and mortals don't know the real truth, but to me a Golem that isn't clay is like a Vampire that dosen't drink blood or a Werewolf that can't shapeshift. Some things are just integral to the concept.<br /> <br /> Now that said - my ideal situation would be one where Lineages are narrowly defined and extremely specific - but Promethian's <i>don't know that</i>. So all Golems are made of Clay, but a Golem experiments with creating a Tammuz out of flesh and succeeds. That's two different (but very very similar - identical in everything except the flesh/clay) Lineages - but members of both lineages consider themselves to be the same lineage. Only highly experienced Ophidians know the truth, and even they realise that while technically metaphysically wrong, culturally they're the same Lineage and culturally is more important than metaphysically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:49:32-07:00","id":274221,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that Tammuz aren't only based on the clay golem myth - the name itself refers to the Babylonian myth of Ishtar/Inanna's descent into the Underworld to resurrect her lover from the earth (not unlike the Osirian origin myth - same basic idea of a fertility figure who died to be reborn, representing the turning of the year).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T16:07:10-07:00","id":274234,"title":"","content":"If I'm honest, I'd prefer it if they focused more on the clay Golem myth - which they might well be given the focus on language that Matt has mentioned before. We already have one fertility god coming back from the dead; more diversity instead of a second.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which. I would love something about Osiris and Isis as NPCs. Preferably options, one of which should be WoD Empyrean; an unsterilised part of the setting and one that should interact nicely with the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T16:57:38-07:00","id":274272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/273240-ptc-2e-open-development-has-started?p=274183#post274183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also hope Golems aren't corpses, since that's antithetical to the source material. At the very least, I hope that Golems from clay are a viable option in the new core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and they've never strayed from the source material and been better for it.<br /> <br /> Cough.<br /> <br /> EDIT: All of this is actually kind of irrelevant. While I don't know by first hand(I haven't read the document) or even second hand(I've been told by someone), I can guarantee you that at most, it's going to be either/or, and I don't place high odds on that-it'll probably be the corpse bodies barring the Unfleshed. I'm cool with that.<br /> <br /> The corpse is much more of the point anyways.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also worth noting: I'm also the asshole who hoped that the most hoped for option in regards to the new game wouldn't even come close to coming true, so, you know, keep that in mind in this conversation-I am a genuine asshole on stuff like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-06-2014, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T18:13:58-07:00","id":274333,"title":"","content":"Promethean, to me, is this weird love story of a human for humanity. If there's a piece of media that strikes the same chords in me that Promethean does, it's - oddly enough - the remade Battlestar Galactica, especially themes of whether or not humanity is worthy of survival and how adversity brings out both the best and the worst in people. I also tend to associate alchemy with Zork Nemesis, which was the first time I'd been properly introduced to the concepts of alchemy in media. Consequently, the concept of Western alchemy is irrevocably linked to string music for me, so I listened to almost nothing but the string-heavy BSG soundtracks while writing for Promethean. If people end up looping <a href=\"http://youtu.be/HG-Js_rMEV4?list=PL298FC37751CB5B01\" target=\"_blank\">Roslin and Adama</a> while reading the book, I think it'd work just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 10-06-2014, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T18:52:06-07:00","id":274356,"title":"","content":"Aside from the ability to be more true to the original myths, one reason I\u2019m hoping that Constructs are a thing in 2e is the following excerpt from <b>Magnum Opus</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Some players have difficulty with the primary theme of Promethean: attaining Humanity as a driving goal. Unlike vampire, mage and werewolf characters, the Created do not begin as human and then gain supernatural powers. Although the creation mechanics begin by creating a human being and adding supernatural, the in-character premise is quite different. Prometheans have not \u201cgone beyond\u201d humanity \u2014 they never had it. By striving to attain their Mortality, they are not giving up being super-human. They are transitioning from less-than-human to human.<br /> <br /> It may be difficult for a player to avoid thinking of his character as super-human if every Promethean character he has created or encountered was made from a human corpse. Especially for players who are familiar with <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, the idea of Prometheans as former humans is a difficult one to avoid. An encounter with a statue-turned-Aphrodite or a wood-carving-made-Riven may cement the concept that regardless of where their bodies came from, no Promethean is ever truly human before her Magnum Opus.</span></div>Granted, the inclusion of the Unfleshed helps immensely in this regard. OTOH,<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Just as any legend, the tale of Galatea and Pygmalion has undergone countless retellings over the centuries. In some, Pygmalion is a king, in others, only a lonely artist. Some place the tale in Cyprus, some Rome and one legend on the island of Atlantis before its destruction. Some stories speak of the sculptor summoning forth his creation from stone, others from ivory or even wax. But the one factor that all variations of the human myth of Galatea share is that she was carved or crafted out of something inanimate, the product of an artist, not a grave-robber.</span></div>For this reason if no other, I\u2019d like Galeteids to be able to be crafted by artists. Picking a corpse that\u2019s unblemished just isn\u2019t the same as breathing life into a work of art that you crafted yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T00:32:03-07:00","id":274531,"title":"","content":"While I like the quest for humanity and am fine with it remaining the core/default option for Promethian; I would very much like it if there was a book (perhaps the Equinox Roads equivalent) about alternatives to the Pilgrimage. By which I mean epic quests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"u